    "role": {
      "type": "layer-stack",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "dark",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Restore means supporting the systems skin relies on.",
        "body": "<p>Skin is constantly responding to:</p><ul><li>Environmental stress</li><li>Normal oxidative processes</li><li>Nutritional demands</li><li>Immune signaling</li><li>Daily renewal</li></ul><p>“Restore” does not mean repairing every form of damage or reversing aging. Within the Alchemia MD system, it means providing nutritional support for the biological systems involved in maintaining calm, balanced, resilient skin.†</p>",
        "callout": "Protect responds to exposure. Balance supports the gut and internal balance.† Restore supports antioxidant, nutritional, and immune pathways.†"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "b1": {
          "type": "layer",
          "settings": {
            "short": "Protect",
            "title": "Protect",
            "text": "Respond to environmental exposure."
          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "layer",
          "settings": {
            "short": "Balance",
            "title": "Balance",
            "text": "Support gut-skin and internal balance.†"
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "layer",
          "settings": {
            "short": "Restore",
            "title": "Restore",
            "text": "Support antioxidant, nutritional, and immune pathways involved in everyday skin resilience.†"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "b1",
        "b2",
        "b3"
      ]
    },
    "antioxidant": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "green",
        "align": "left",
        "width": "wide",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Oxidative stress is not one single pathway.",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "body": "<p>Reactive molecules are produced as part of normal metabolism and can also increase in response to environmental stress. The body relies on multiple antioxidant systems to maintain balance.†</p><p>That is one reason Dermaboost+ does not depend on a single antioxidant. Its formulation includes several chemically distinct compounds:</p><ul><li>Vitamin C</li><li>Quercetin</li><li>Curcumin</li><li>Olive leaf polyphenols</li><li>Astaxanthin</li><li>Niacinamide</li></ul><p>Different compounds can behave differently within cellular environments, which is the rationale for combining multiple nutritional and botanical sources rather than positioning one ingredient as a complete solution.</p>",
        "quote": "Antioxidant support is part of normal nutritional physiology, not a promise to eliminate oxidative stress."
      }
    },
    "formula": {
      "type": "product-actives",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "green",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Ingredients",
        "columns": "4"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "b1": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Niacinamide",
            "amount": "250 mg NE per serving",
            "role": "Cellular + barrier support",
            "slide_set": "",
            "text": "<p>Niacinamide is a form of vitamin B3 involved in cellular energy metabolism and skin-related biological processes.</p><p>Within Dermaboost+, it contributes a nutritional mechanism distinct from the formula’s botanical polyphenols and carotenoids.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore niacinamide research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#niacinamide"
          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Vitamin D3",
            "amount": "25 mcg (1,000 IU) per serving",
            "role": "Normal immune function",
            "slide_set": "",
            "text": "<p>Vitamin D plays established physiological roles in immune regulation and numerous cellular processes.</p><p>Dermaboost+ includes vitamin D3 as part of its broader nutritional support strategy.†</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore vitamin D research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#vitamin-d3"
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Vitamin C",
            "amount": "45 mg per serving",
            "role": "Antioxidant + collagen-related nutrition",
            "slide_set": "",
            "text": "<p>Vitamin C is an essential nutrient and antioxidant. It also serves as a required cofactor in normal collagen synthesis.</p><p>Its role in Dermaboost+ is foundational nutritional support.†</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore vitamin C research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#vitamin-c"
          }
        },
        "b4": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Zinc",
            "amount": "5 mg per serving",
            "role": "Immune + cellular support",
            "slide_set": "",
            "text": "<p>Zinc is an essential mineral involved in normal immune function, protein synthesis, DNA synthesis, and numerous enzyme systems.</p><p>Within the formula, it complements vitamin C and vitamin D as part of the nutritional foundation.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore zinc research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#zinc"
          }
        },
        "b5": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Quercetin",
            "amount": "250 mg per serving",
            "role": "Polyphenol antioxidant support",
            "slide_set": "",
            "text": "<p>Quercetin is a plant flavonoid studied for antioxidant activity and cellular-signaling effects.</p><p>Within Dermaboost+, it contributes a different polyphenolic profile from curcumin and olive leaf extract.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore quercetin research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#quercetin"
          }
        },
        "b6": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Optimized curcumin",
            "amount": "300 mg per serving",
            "role": "Botanical antioxidant support",
            "text": "<p>Curcumin is a botanical polyphenol widely studied for antioxidant and cell-signaling activity.</p><p>The formulation uses an optimized form to address curcumin’s naturally limited oral bioavailability.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore curcumin research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#curcumin"
          }
        },
        "b7": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Olive leaf extract",
            "amount": "150 mg per serving",
            "role": "Polyphenol support",
            "text": "<p>Olive leaf contains polyphenols including oleuropein.</p><p>Within Dermaboost+, it adds another botanical source of antioxidant and signaling-related activity to the formula’s broader nutrient network.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore olive leaf research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#dermaboost"
          }
        },
        "b8": {
          "type": "active",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Astaxanthin",
            "amount": "4 mg per serving",
            "role": "Carotenoid antioxidant support",
            "text": "<p>Astaxanthin is a carotenoid antioxidant studied in human research involving several skin-related parameters.</p><p>It provides a structurally different antioxidant component from the vitamins and polyphenols in Dermaboost+.</p>",
            "link_label": "Explore astaxanthin research",
            "link_url": "/pages/science#astaxanthin",
            "slide_set": ""
          }
        }
      },
