    "immune": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "light",
        "align": "left",
        "width": "wide",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Skin is part of the immune system’s front line.",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "body": "<p>Skin is not simply a covering. It contains immune cells and participates in communication between the body and the outside environment. Normal immune function therefore matters to skin health.</p><p>Dermaboost+ includes nutrients with established roles in normal immune physiology, including:</p><ul><li>Vitamin D3</li><li>Vitamin C</li><li>Zinc</li></ul><p>alongside antioxidant and botanical compounds selected for complementary nutritional support.†</p>",
        "quote": "Supporting normal immune function is not the same as treating immune-mediated disease."
      }
    },
    "collagen": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "light",
        "align": "left",
        "width": "wide",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Collagen requires nutritional support.",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "body": "<p>Collagen is one of the primary structural proteins in skin. Vitamin C is required for normal collagen synthesis.</p><p>Other Dermaboost+ ingredients have been investigated in relation to oxidative pathways that can influence skin structure. That research describes biology; it is not a promise about specific outcomes.</p>",
        "quote": "Support for normal biology, without overpromising outcomes."
      }
    },
